Adopted-AK-SS-Standards-2024_09c1fb.pdf: K-2 and 3-5 inquiry standards (u392-u431, u977-u1025) and 6-8 inquiry standards (u1666-u1715) are band-level skills standards; labeled with the full band (K-2, 3-5, 6-8) so they are copied into each grade. 9-12 inquiry (u2552-u2627) labeled course null, grades 9-12.
Adopted-AK-SS-Standards-2024_09c1fb.pdf: Grade 6, 7, 8 are grade-level (course null) even though each has a thematic title (Grade 6 Alaska Studies and Geography; Grade 7 World History and Geography; Grade 8 U.S. History and Civics). Grades 9-12 discipline sections (Civics, Economics, Geography, Alaska History, U.S. History, World History) were treated as courses per the state guide, course = discipline name from the section title ('Grade 9 through 12 Civics Standards' -> 'Civics'); the section headings u2629, u2691, u2743, u2787, u3154, u3624 are labeled with that course.
Adopted-AK-SS-Standards-2024_09c1fb.pdf: Page 114-125 tables (U.S. History theme 1 and World History theme 1: u3157-u3186, u3627-u3667) are shifted one column right (Topic in C2, anchor in C3, standards in C4); handled by cell text, grades unaffected. u3166 ('Alaska Government') and u3646 ('14') are continuation fragments of anchor labels; labeled standards.
Adopted-AK-SS-Standards-2024_09c1fb.pdf: Source code oddities (not corrected, labels unaffected): SS.8.1.16.1 appears twice in Grade 8 (u2127, u2154); SS.8.8.21.1 twice (u2522, u2530); SS.8.7.4.1 listed under History Anchor 24 (u2472); SS.USH.23.9.1 (u3198) and SS.USH.17.9.1 (u3209) have malformed codes; Grade 8 topic 'Civic Participation' (u2214) is attached to a History Anchor 24 row; Grade 7 topic u1922 reads 'Prehistory (formerly human environment interaction)'; Grade 7 u2084 etc. topic 'Conquest and Conquer' as written."
