Grade Level Themes
Grade 2
Overcoming Obstacles: Responding to the Challenges We Face
Civics
Knowledge and Skill Performance Expectations
Grade 2
C.1.2.1 Identify founding documents of the United States: ● Declaration of Independence* ● U.S. Constitution* ● Bill of Rights*
C.1.2.2 Describe and classify roles and responsibilities of people in authority in communities which may include: ● School district: school superintendent and school board ● City: mayor and city council ● State: governor and General Assembly ● Nation: President and Congress
C.1.2.3 Explain the functions of government using local examples such as infrastructure, safety, and rules/laws.
Civics
Grade 2
C.1.2.4 Explain the significance of state and national symbols, patriotic songs, and mottos: ● American flag ● Flag etiquette ● Star Spangled Banner ● Recitation of Pledge of Allegiance* ● National Motto: In God we Trust* ● State Seal ● Diana fritillary butterfly ● Fiddle ● Quartz ● Bauxite ● Pink Tomato
C.1.2.5 Describe roles and responsibilities of individuals in a democracy.
C.1.2.6 Discuss ways to build a consensus with a group when making a decision that can bring about change.
