Understanding the expectation of instruction – whenever there is a list of specific items included within a benchmark, educators need to understand the difference between a list preceded by e.g., and one that begins with i.e.
• e.g. means that these are suggestions of people, places or concepts that can be included in instruction. It may help to think of this as a “for example” list. • i.e. refers to people, places or concepts that must, at a minimum, be included in instruction. It may help to think of this as “all-inclusive” or “include all.”
