o Two main types of plays:
 Tragedies: Serious themes about human suffering
and moral lessons
 Comedies: Lighthearted plays that mocked politics,
society, and well-known citizens.
• Philosophy: Socrates, Plato, and Aristotle explored ethics,
politics, and knowledge
May include: • Persian Wars: United Greek city-states defeated Persia, leading to pride and Athens’ rise. • Peloponnesian War: Rivalry between Athens and Sparta led to conflict; Sparta won but Greece was weakened and divided.
