Must include, but is not limited to: • Written Laws (Primary source for this sub theme may include The Twelve Tables). • Rule of Law: Laws applied equally to all citizens. • Government Structure: The idea of separation of government powers into branches. • Concept of Citizenship: Rights and responsibilities of citizens in a government. • The Three Branches of Government in the Roman Republic: o Consuls — Two leaders who ran the government and army o Senate — A group of wealthy, powerful men who made laws and advised the consuls o Assemblies — Groups of Roman citizens who voted on laws and leaders
