Members of the Meskwaki Nation live on a sovereign settlement in Iowa, not a reservation. The Meskwaki Nation is independent from the state government of Iowa. They are governed by their own constitution, codified laws and an elected seven-member Tribal Council that oversees the tribal school, tribal courts, and other services on the settlement.
Diplomats, politicians, and political analysts evaluate, and interpret political trends, policies, and events to provide recommendations for government, organizations, or the public.
May include, but not limited to: • Characteristics of folk culture • Ways people depend on the environment • Relationship between culture and people’s perceptions of places and regions • People create regions to interpret Earth’s complexity
