HS.WH.KH.1 Describe the impact of world history on Kentuckians and how Kentucky impacted the world. HS.WH.KH.1 Describe the impact of world history on Kentuckians and how Kentucky impacted the world.
Many Kentuckians have contributed to legislative efforts, reform movements, and global conflicts and compromises in impactful ways. Some examples include, but are not limited to: Cassius Marcellus Clay served as United States Minister to Russia where he was instrumental in ensuring that Russia did not recognize the South as an independent nation; Muhammed Ali became a global influence as a result of his fight for civil rights and humanitarian work; Dr. Lilialyce Akers served the United Nations in many roles, including a representative to the Commission on Women; Mary Willie Arvin was a nurse who received honors from three allied countries for service during World War I.
