Standards for History and Social Science Practice, Pre-K–12*18 1. Demonstrate civic knowledge, skills, and dispositions. 2. Develop focused questions or problem statements and conduct inquiries. 3. Organize information and data from multiple primary and secondary sources. 4. Analyze the purpose and point of view of each source; distinguish opinion from fact. 5. Evaluate the credibility, accuracy, and relevance of each source. 6. Argue or explain conclusions, using valid reasoning and evidence. 7. Determine next steps and take
