Selected responses by Anti-Federalists (1787–1789) 16. The Federal Farmer (Richard Henry Lee) and Centinel These two documents are included in a National Endowment for the Humanities curriculum unit on the debates between Federalists and anti-Federalists (see also http://oll.libertyfund.org/?option=com staticxt&staticfile=show.php%3Ftitle=690&chapter=1023 _ 13&layout=html&Itemid=27, and http://www.teachingamericanhistory.com/library/index.asp?document=1635 and https://edsitement.neh.gov/curriculum-unit/federalist-and-anti-federalist-debates-diversity-and- extended-republic)
68. Justice Robert M. Jackson: Opinion for the Supreme Court in West Virginia State Board of Education v. Barnette (1943) The Supreme Court ruled that students are protected from having to salute the flag or recite the Pledge of Allegiance under the free exercise clause of the First Amendment (see also https://www.oyez.org/cases/1940-1955/319us624)
