55 Mendez v. Westminster School District of Orange County, California (1946) is regarded as a precedent for the Brown challenge to “separate but equal” schools. In this California class action suit, Mexican Americans sued to dismantle California’s system of schools segregated on the basis of national origin. See Mendez v. Westminster: Desegregating California’s Schools, a video interview with Sylvia Mendez, historians, and legal scholars. (see also https://mass.pbslearningmedia.org/resource/osi04.soc.ush.civil.mendez/mendez-v-westminster-desegregating-californias- schools/#.Wwwd8BqWzIV)
