[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] STRANDS: CIVICS, ECONOMICS, CIVIL RIGHTS, GEOGRAPHY, AND HISTORY
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] STANDARD
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] OBJECTIVE(S)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] HAME.1 Contrast how geography, economics, and politics have influenced the development of the ancient Middle East. (Strands: Civics, Civil Rights, Geography, History, Economics)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] 2. Examine the advantages of living in a river valley or coastal region as compared to inland areas of the Middle East. 3. Describe major events in the development and decline of regional empires, including: Egyptian, Assyrian, Babylonian, Medo-Persian, Greek and Roman. 4. Examine the development of Israel as a civilization.
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] HAME.2 Trace the relationship of people, places, and environments throughout time. (Strands: Civics, Civil Rights, Geography, History, Economics)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] 2. Analyze the accomplishments and failures of key people of the Middle East from 2000 B.C. to 100 A.D. 3. Critique the conflicts over the land of Palestine from 2000 B.C. to 100 A.D. 4. Analyze the movements and interactions of various groups of people in the ancient Middle East. 5. Discuss the impact of war and conflict on different groups from 2000 B.C. to 100 A.D.
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] HAME.3 Examine the contributions made by archaeological work in the Middle East. (Strands: Civics, Civil Rights, Geography, History, Economics)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] 1. Define the science of archaeology. 2. Review archaeological finds in the Middle East. 3. Critique the impact of archaeology related to various documents, including: Hammurabi’s Code, the Bible, Dead Sea scrolls, etc.
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] HAME.4 Describe the impact of science and technology on the historical development of the Middle East. (Strands: Civics, Civil Rights, Geography, History, Economics)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] 1. Explain how technological development transformed agriculture and customs of the ancient Middle East. 2. Describe the transition from the barter system to monetary system, including: coinage, etc.
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] HAME.5 Demonstrate the ability to apply and interpret social studies tools, including: timelines, maps, globes, graphs, compass, technology, political cartoons, primary and secondary documents, charts, etc. (Strands: Civics, Civil Rights, Geography, History, Economics)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] 1. Locate and label selected physical features of the Middle East. 2. Compare and contrast ancient political boundaries with those of modern independent nations.
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] HAME.6 Debate the similarities and differences of ancient Middle Eastern cultures. (Strands: Civics, Civil Rights, Geography, History, Economics)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] 1. Compare and contrast the religious practices, rituals, and traditions of ancient Middle Eastern cultures. 2. Analyze examples of cultural contributions made by various ancient civilizations of the Middle East. 3. Examine the roles, status, and interaction of diverse groups of people, including: parents, children, men, women, slaves, etc.within various ancient Middle Eastern societies. 4. Analyze selected examples of ancient Middle Eastern literature, including: legends, poetry, prophecy, and wisdom literature, etc.
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] HAME.7 Analyze the development of social and political systems in the ancient Middle East. (Strands: Civics, Civil Rights, Geography, History, Economics)
[HISTORY OF THE ANCIENT MIDDLE EAST, 2000 B.C. TO 1000 A.D.] 13. Compare/contrast political systems of the ancient Middle East. 14. Discuss major political movements from 2000 B.C. to 100 A.D. 15. Describe the warfare, weaponry, and resolution of conflicts in the ancient Middle East. 16. Analyze the development and expansion of various legal systems, including: Hebrew, Roman, Sumerian, Egyptian, etc. 17. Show the impact of various empires on developing social structures of the ancient Middle East. 18. Summarize the effects of early religious teachings on ancient and modern social structures, including: Hebrew, Christian, Roman, Persian, and Egyptian.
