pictures, posters, oral/written narratives, and electronic presentation","Middle School Standards Introduction: The purpose of Nebraska’s 6-8 Social Studies Standards is to integrate important subject matter and skills, and to provide students a robust understanding of grade-specific concepts. The standards should not be viewed in isolation, but as a unifying approach to social studies curriculum and instruction.",Nebraska-Social-Studies-Standards-Final-11-2019_bc9931.pdf,"Nebraska-Social-Studies-Standards-Final-11-2019_bc9931.pdf: Extraction is table-fragmented throughout: many standards and their 'For example' text are split across table-cell units (e.g. u86-u90, u100-u103, u738-u745, u946-u957). Units with no SS code or 'For example' marker were labeled by position: fragments following a 'For example' unit (or whose 'For example:' prefix was lost, e.g. u758-u759, u772-u775, u866-u867, u877, u905-u909, u971-u975, u1024-u1026, u1130-u1132, u1288-u1290) are labeled examples; continuations of standard text (e.g. u102, u177, u202, u274, u370, u476-u477, u615, u739-u742) are labeled standards.
