Nebraska-Social-Studies-Standards-Final-11-2019_bc9931.pdf: u90, u202, u236, u1407: mixed or fragmentary units labeled standards (u90 is a duplicate cut-off copy of K.4.1.b; u236 contains the end of SS 2.2.4.b plus its example; u1407 is the World History course heading).
Nebraska-Social-Studies-Standards-Final-11-2019_bc9931.pdf: Units that combine a standard with its 'For example' text (very common, e.g. u59, u73, u119, u1228, and most HS units) are labeled standards (units not split). Units combining several indicators (e.g. u73, u306, u390, u1307, u1322, u1331, u1338) cover multiple codes.
Nebraska-Social-Studies-Standards-Final-11-2019_bc9931.pdf: Grade Level Summary and Theme / HS 'Summary' units (u35, u116, u208, u302, u395, u509, u735, u893, u1094, u1282, u1313, u1352, u1384) mix the theme title with a content narrative and some end with the discipline heading (e.g. 'Civics'); labeled examples (narrative describing what students study) rather than standards. Alternative: standards for the theme title.
Nebraska-Social-Studies-Standards-Final-11-2019_bc9931.pdf: State guide lists HS topics as Civics, Economics, Geography, History strands; the document has no separate HS courses: HS standards are one 9-12 band organized by discipline (SS HS.1.x Civics, HS.2.x Economics, HS.3.x Geography, HS.4.x History). Civics, Economics, Geography labeled course null, grades 9-12; the History strand has two course-like sub-sections coded (US) and (WLD), labeled course 'United States History (Progressive Era – Present)' and 'World History (1500 CE – Present)' (u1385-u1406, u1407-u1423); the History strand title/summary (u1383-u1384) are course null.
