NV_06-08_PersonalFinance,NV,"[6,7,8]",Personal Finance,Economics,Financial Literacy,"Content Themes
Grades 6-8: Financial Literacy
Financial decision- making (FL)
Financial decision-
SS.6-8.FL.1. Prioritize and evaluate personal finance goals based on needs and wants. SS.6-8.FL.2. Investigate consequences of potential financial decisions to make reasoned financial choices. SS.6-8.FL.3. Describe the services offered by various financial institutions, and government agencies, including but not limited to: Matching Grant Money for College, Prepaid College Tuition, and 529 College Savings Plan.
making (FL)
Savings and spending
SS.6-8.FL.4. Discuss the components of a personal budget - including income, planned spending, expenses, and saving.
(FL)
Credit and debt (FL)
Credit and debt (FL)
SS.6-8.FL.5. Explain how debit cards differ from credit cards. SS.6-8.FL.6. Explain an individual’s rights and responsibilities as a consumer. SS.6-8.FL.7. Discuss the cost of borrowing money for different types of goods and services, including but not limited to: consumables, vehicles, higher education, and housing.
Insurance, investing,
SS.6-8.FL.8. Investigate ways to prevent and limit the consequences of identity theft and fraud. SS.6-8.FL.9. Explain how some investments differ from traditional savings accounts in potential risks and returns.
and risk (FL)
