SPATIAL THINKING AND SKILLS PLACES AND REGIONS Content Statements: Content Statements: 4. Physical and political maps have distinctive characteristics and 5. Daily life is influenced by the agriculture, industry and natural purposes. Places can be located on a map by using the title, resources in different communities. key, alphanumeric grid and cardinal directions. HUMAN SYSTEMS Content Statements: 6. Evidence of positive and negative human modification of the environment can be observed in the local community. 7. Systems of transportation and communication move people, products and ideas from place to place. 8. Communities may include diverse cultural groups.
PLACES AND REGIONS
