Grade 3, continued
GOVERNMENT STRAND
CIVIC PARTICIPATION AND SKILLS RULES AND LAWS Content Statement: Content Statement: 9. Members of local communities have rights and responsibilities. 11. Laws are rules which apply to all people in a community and 10. Individuals make the community a better place by taking action describe ways people are expected to behave. Laws promote to solve problems in a way that promotes the common good. order and security, provide public services and protect the rights of individuals in the local community. ROLES AND SYSTEMS OF GOVERNMENT Content Statement: 12. Governments have authority to make and enforce laws. 13. The structure of local governments may differ from one community to another.
