Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Analyze ways throughout time people have adapted to living in different environments (e.g., mountains, deserts, rainforests, woodlands, cold climates, warm climates) b. Explain that different environments provide different resources for human habitation, and analyze how that can encourage human settlement c. Explain types of natural disasters (e.g., hurricanes, floods, blizzards, drought, wildfires), and analyze how they can affect human settlement and population d. Analyze ways that natural disasters can change the economic situation of people (e.g., destruction of property, access to food sources, access to clean water) e. Analyze environmental situations that may cause people to migrate (e.g., migration away from a location to escape a natural disaster, migration to a location that has access to more resources) f. Analyze ways recent changes in the Earth’s climate have affected various communities (e.g., erosion and flooding of coastal Alaskan villages, droughts in the Western United States)
