Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Identify the causes and course of the French and Indian War, and argue how it impacted the colonies b. Analyze the roles and contributions Indigenous peoples had in the French and Indian War c. Analyze the Proclamation of 1763 and other acts of the British government meant to recoup financial costs of the French and Indian War (e.g., Sugar Act 1764, Currency Act 1764, Stamp Act 1765, Townshend Act 1767) and assert control over the colonies (e.g., Quartering Act 1765, Coercive Acts 1774) and argue how these led to the start of the Revolution d. Analyze protests and major events leading up to the American Revolution (e.g., Boston Massacre, Gaspee Affair, Stamp Act riots, North Carolina Regulators, various Tea Parties), and argue how these led to the start of Revolution
