Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Analyze how liberty and natural rights are defined in the Declaration of Independence b. Analyze the grievances and ideals laid out in the Declaration of Independence c. Analyze the backgrounds (race, gender, occupation, religion, age, location, and view of slavery) of the Declaration of Independence signatories, and explain their perspectives and political views (e.g., Rhode Island’s Stephen Hopkins and William Ellery) d. Analyze the influences of the Haudenosaunee Confederacy on the drafting of the Declaration of Independence (e.g., Great League of Peace) e. Explain ways that students see the ideals of the Declaration of Independence represented in their lives today
