Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Analyze the definition of the Transportation Revolution, and argue its impact on the United States (e.g., steamboats, canals, roads, bridges, turnpikes, railroads) b. Analyze the events of the Industrial Revolution, and argue how the shift from an agricultural to industrial economy shaped daily life prior to the Civil War (e.g., Slater Mill in Rhode Island, Rhode Island System, Lowell Mill Girls, child labor, technological developments) c. Analyze other industries, and argue their influence on the United States (e.g., whaling, shipping, international trade)
