Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Identify ways to express the scale of time (e.g., decade, age, era, century, millennium, BCE, CE) and explain why times periods are named differently in different contexts b. Identify terms for historical periods (e.g., Paleolithic Era, Neolithic Era, Before Common Era, Common Era) and the time we are living in now c. Identify linear and comparative timelines, and explain how to read and use them
