Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Identify the characteristics of a complex society (e.g., economy that produces food surplus and ability to store food surplus, specialized jobs, systems for government, religion, art, technology) and analyze how those characteristics influenced social life b. Analyze the impacts of the development of agriculture and herding on populations c. Analyze the interaction between and spread of complex societies (e.g., migration, trade, agriculture, exchange of culture and/or language, religious conversion, colonization) d. Explain the significance of the Fertile Crescent, identify its location, and analyze the role of natural resources in its development e. Analyze the influence of geography on the development of the social, economic, and political structure of Indigenous civilizations in the Americas
