Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Explain the differences between “citizenship” as it pertains to being an active and responsible participant in any community or group and legal citizenship b. Analyze the changes in how legal citizenship has been defined over time, and argue the impacts and who has benefited c. Explain the responsibilities of being an active and responsible participant in a community d. Analyze the barriers to full participation as citizens, and argue who benefits from them e. Analyze instances when citizenship has been challenged or denied, and argue who benefited
