Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Analyze the definition of and the rationale for federalism, and argue who benefited from that system b. Analyze the arguments and rationales found in the Federalist Papers, and argue who benefited (Suggested Federalist Papers – 9, 10, 39, 51, 70, 78, 84) c. Analyze the distinctions between the Virginia and New Jersey plans, and argue who benefited under each plan d. Analyze the impact of the Constitution on different groups in American society, and argue who benefited e. Analyze the reasons why Rhode Island refused to send a delegate to the Constitutional Convention
