Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Explain the origin of and arguments made in Common Sense b. Identify the nature and conditions of colonial grievances against King George III in the Declaration of Independence c. Analyze the efficacy of enlightenment ideas evident in founding documents (e.g., social contract, natural rights, separation of powers) d. Analyze the rationale behind the removal of the anti-slavery passage in the Declaration of Independence, and argue who benefited and the impacts of that action e. Analyze the range of colonial responses to the Declaration of Independence based on one’s positionality (e.g., Frederick Douglass, Abigail Adams, Patriots, Loyalists) f. Analyze the uses of the Declaration of Independence in the colonial cause, and argue its impact
