Learning Assessment Objectives: Students demonstrate an ability to: a. Analyze the relationships between caste groups (e.g., Brahmin, Kshatriyas, Vaishyas, Sudras), and argue the impact on society and who benefited b. Analyze the individual jobs, wealth, and access to resources based on caste distinction c. Analyze the development of social standards through Hindu beliefs (e.g., Samsara, Karma, Dharma) d. Argue the impact Hinduism had on the maintenance of the rigidity of the caste system e. Argue the impact Hinduism had on the development of city-states and empires f. Analyze the development of Buddhism and the Eightfold path g. Analyze the similarities and differences between the practices and ideas of Hinduism and Buddhism (e.g., perspectives on god, morality, human nature)
