Causation
Analyze patterns of continuities and changes within U. S. history through the use of evidence from a variety of sources, such as graphic organizers, maps, photographs/images, texts, and timelines.
Continuities and
Changes
Evaluate different forms of evidence used in historical inquiry and determine their validity.
Evidence
Geography Skills
Grade 2
Describe and compare various landforms over time within the U. S. through the use of primary and secondary sources. .
Maps
Identify the geographic location of the U.S. in relation to the rest of the world.
Gather Evidence and
Communicate Findings
Explain how the distribution of human features, physical features, and natural resources in the U. S. impact economic activity.
Conditions and
Connections
Economic Skills
Grade 2
Examine the purpose of currency and how income, savings, and spending are parts of a budget
Establish Relationships
Explain how budgets change as wants and needs or the availability of goods and services change.
Interpret
Create a simple budget and articulate the priorities using economic terms such as expenses, income, and savings.
Communicate and
Conclude
Interpret data to show how geographic location and available resources impact economic decision- making.
Informed Participation
Civics and Government Skills
Grade 2
Identify cultural and ethnic groups in the U.S., explore their characteristics, and communicate how civic dispositions build relationships between groups in a diverse society.
Establish
Relationships
Use primary and secondary sources to research a national figure who demonstrated civic dispositions.
Interpret
Analyze how rights are granted to U.S. citizens through the founding documents.
Communicate &
Conclude
Use evidence to propose and communicate a resolution to a national issue.
