C, E, G, H, P, T
Statehood and Early History (1796-1849) Overview: Students will examine the process of Tennessee becoming a state, study the importance of Andrew Jackson and his presidency, and discuss important Tennesseans of the era.
5.10
Sequence events that led to Tennessee statehood, including ""The Lost State of Franklin,” the Southwest Territory (i.e., Territory South of the River Ohio), and the U.S. Constitutional requirements Tennessee met to become a state. (T.C.A. § 49-6- 1028)
