about U.S. history by studying amendments to the Constitution?
By the end of the 19th century, global and domestic events led the U.S. to reconsider the advan tages of isolation versus intervention in world affairs. The U.S. increased its role in the world and became enmeshed in global conflicts. Decisions related to isolationism and interventionism continue to be made today.
