World War II transformed American society and redefined the United States’ role in global af fairs. The war produced unprecedented levels of violence and human suffering. On the home front, trends both during and after the war would shape American society into the 21st cen tury. The post-war era saw America emerge as one of two superpowers, engaged in a global “cold war” with the Soviet Union. This Cold War had implications for America both at home and abroad.
] How did decisions that leaders made during World War II change the rules of warfare?
