what role government and political decision making played in its inception, duration, and resolution.
Economic Thinking Economic investigators are interested in the compari- son of marginal costs and marginal benefits to allocate resources in a manner that maximizes well-being. Although not all economic investigators share the same
A compelling question, then, demands that students
think and reason economically, geographically, histor- ically, and politically (Dimension 2) in order to fully address the issue. Along with the behavioral and social sciences, these disciplinary lenses help students think broadly; separately, these lenses enable students to set up and pursue their investigations in different ways.
