Meira Levinson is associate professor of education at Harvard Uni- versity, where she teaches courses on civic and multicultural education, urban education, social studies methods, and justice in schools. She taught middle school for eight years in low-income schools. Her most recent books include No Citizen Left Behind (2012) and Making Civics Count (2012, co-edited).
